    {"ip": "10.40.5.40", "inferred_role": "finance_file_server_first_use_of_rogue_account", "first_seen": "2026-08-03T01:48:42+0200", "last_seen": "2026-08-03T01:48:42+0200", "agent_name": "FILESVR-FIN-01"}
  ],
  "attack_progression": [
    {"step": 1, "tactic": "Initial Access / Valid Accounts (Hijacked)", "technique": "T1078.002", "what_happened": "At 2026-08-03 01:38:18 CEST (off-hours, weekend night), Windows Security Event 4624 fired on DC-CORP-01.corp.local (10.40.2.10): logonType=10 (RemoteInteractive = RDP), TargetUserName=nadia.r (CORP\\nadia.r — IT admin account), IpAddress=10.40.7.84 (WS-IT-12, her assigned workstation). Source IP + workstation match nadia.r's normal admin-bastion path — the auth itself looks routine. However, the off-hours timing (01:38 on a Saturday night) plus the actions that follow within 4 minutes (rogue admin-account creation, group elevation, no ITSM ticket) indicate the nadia.r account is HIJACKED — likely via stolen credentials, session-token replay, or live attacker access to WS-IT-12.", "chain_reason": "Windows Security Event 4624 (rule.id 60224, level 13) anchors the start of the chain — it is the auth-success that enables the subsequent privileged actions. Linkage: agent.name=DC-CORP-01.corp.local + targetUserName=nadia.r + logonType=10 + ipAddress=10.40.7.84.", "first_seen": "2026-08-03T01:38:18+0200"},
    {"step": 2, "tactic": "Persistence / Create Account (Domain)", "technique": "T1136.001", "what_happened": "At 01:42:11 CEST (~4 minutes after the RDP logon), Windows Security Event 4720 'A user account was created' fired on DC-CORP-01.corp.local: TargetUserName=svc-backup01, TargetDomainName=CORP, SubjectUserName=nadia.r, NewUACList=PASSWD_NOTREQD,NORMAL_ACCOUNT. The account name 'svc-backup01' uses a service-account naming convention (svc-* prefix) typically reserved for non-interactive workloads — but the flag PASSWD_NOTREQD on a service account is a known persistence pattern (account can be reset to any password without policy enforcement). Off-hours creation of a domain-scope service-flavor account by a hijacked IT admin = rogue persistence account stand-up.", "chain_reason": "Windows Security Event 4720 (rule.id 60106) with SubjectUserName=nadia.r ties the creation back to the Step 1 auth-success. Same DC, same actor, ~4 min later. Linkage: agent.name=DC-CORP-01.corp.local + eventID=4720 + subjectUserName=nadia.r + targetUserName=svc-backup01.", "first_seen": "2026-08-03T01:42:11+0200"},
    {"step": 3, "tactic": "Privilege Escalation / Account Manipulation (Domain Admins)", "technique": "T1098", "what_happened": "At 01:42:14 CEST (3 SECONDS after account creation), Windows Security Event 4732 'A member was added to a security-enabled local group' fired on DC-CORP-01.corp.local: TargetUserName=svc-backup01, GroupName=Domain Admins, SubjectUserName=nadia.r, MemberSID=S-1-5-21-...-1234. Adding a freshly-created service-flavor account to Domain Admins within 3 seconds of creation = a SCRIPTED workflow, NOT a human IT-admin workflow. A legitimate IT admin creating a service account would (a) follow ITSM ticket flow, (b) typically NOT add service accounts to Domain Admins (tier-0 violation), (c) NOT execute the two actions within 3 seconds. This is the strongest single signal in the chain.", "chain_reason": "Windows Security Event 4732 with GroupName=Domain Admins + SubjectUserName=nadia.r + TargetUserName=svc-backup01. The 3-second gap between Event 4720 (Step 2) and Event 4732 (Step 3) is the diagnostic temporal signature.", "first_seen": "2026-08-03T01:42:14+0200"},
    {"step": 4, "tactic": "Persistence / Account Manipulation (Password Set)", "technique": "T1098", "what_happened": "At 01:42:18 CEST (4 seconds after the Domain Admins addition), Windows Security Event 4738 'A user account was changed' fired on DC-CORP-01.corp.local: TargetUserName=svc-backup01, PasswordLastSet updated, UserAccountControl changes (likely clearing PASSWD_NOTREQD and setting a controlled password). The attacker is now finalizing the rogue account — guaranteeing they know the password and the account is in a usable state for subsequent authentication.", "chain_reason": "Windows Security Event 4738 (rule.id 60113) with TargetUserName=svc-backup01 + SubjectUserName=nadia.r. 4 seconds after Step 3 → confirms scripted-actor workflow.", "first_seen": "2026-08-03T01:42:18+0200"},
    {"step": 5, "tactic": "Governance / Change-Management Bypass", "technique": "N/A (organizational control)", "what_happened": "At 01:43:02 CEST, Wazuh AD integration decoder (CHANGE_TICKET_LOOKUP) queried the ITSM system for any approved change-request matching 'svc-backup01' OR 'Domain Admins membership change' in the past 30 days: result = NO MATCH. The account creation + privileged group addition has NO change-management approval. This is a hard control-failure indicator: legitimate IT admin work for any privileged group change is gated by a change ticket; the absence of any ticket combined with the off-hours timing rules out 'legitimate emergency admin action'.", "chain_reason": "Wazuh custom rule (corp_ad_change_no_ticket, level 12) matches when a 4720/4732/4738 event on a DC has no corresponding ITSM ticket. Tied to the same SubjectUserName=nadia.r + TargetUserName=svc-backup01 tuple.", "first_seen": "2026-08-03T01:43:02+0200"},
    {"step": 6, "tactic": "Lateral Movement / Test Usage of Rogue Account", "technique": "T1078.002 + T1021.002", "what_happened": "At 01:48:42 CEST (~6.5 minutes after account creation), Windows Security Event 4624 fired on FILESVR-FIN-01: logonType=3 (Network), TargetUserName=svc-backup01, AuthenticationPackageName=Kerberos. This is the FIRST observed usage of the rogue account — a network logon (likely SMB share access or remote management) against the finance file server. The 6.5-minute gap between creation and first use is the attacker's 'test-drive' of their new persistence — verifying Domain Admins membership grants the expected access before pursuing high-value targets. Finance file server as first target = potential interest in financial data (ransomware staging, BEC fraud reconnaissance, or pre-exfiltration).", "chain_reason": "Windows Security Event 4624 on FILESVR-FIN-01 with TargetUserName=svc-backup01 + AuthenticationPackageName=Kerberos. Linked to the same svc-backup01 created in Step 2-4. 6.5-minute gap = attacker validation, not benign software flow.", "first_seen": "2026-08-03T01:48:42+0200"}
  ],
